# Pinned Vector revisions under test.
#
# These are exact commit SHAs, not branch names, so the test result is
# reproducible: a branch moves, a SHA does not. Both are reachable from the
# fork that carries the fix.
#
#   BEFORE -- the fix branch's merge base with vectordotdev/master. Identical to
#             AFTER except for the socket sink finalization fix, so the sink is
#             the only variable. Expected to LOSE lines on reset.
#   AFTER  -- the tip of the fix branch. Expected to lose NOTHING.
#
# Update these when rebasing the PR, and re-record the results in the README.

VECTOR_REPO="${VECTOR_REPO:-https://github.com/simdugas/vector.git}"

# Both SHAs can be overridden from the environment for a one-off run against
# different commits, without editing this file:
#
#   BEFORE_SHA=<base> AFTER_SHA=<fix> ./run_comparison.sh
#
# When overriding AFTER_SHA, set BEFORE_SHA to that commit's merge base with
# master ('git merge-base <after> origin/master'). Pairing a rebased or merged
# fix against a stale base folds unrelated master changes into the comparison,
# which no longer isolates the socket sink.

# Merge base of the fix branch with vectordotdev/master, i.e. the same tree as
# AFTER minus the socket sink changes.
BEFORE_SHA="${BEFORE_SHA:-711f03abce4f7a65e3a84b8893be60675a8aef39}"

# Head of PR #25132 (simdugas/vector fix-tcp-server-reset-issue) as of the
# results recorded in README.md. Bump this to the new head whenever the branch
# gains commits -- and move BEFORE_SHA to the new merge base at the same time --
# then re-run ./run_comparison.sh to refresh those results.
AFTER_SHA="${AFTER_SHA:-1238ca45cd52ee7f4323a95607d0693f0e29c454}"

# Feature set required by the harness config: a file source, a file sink for
# the ground-truth tee, and the socket sink under test. Building without
# default features keeps the build far cheaper than a full Vector.
VECTOR_FEATURES="sources-file,sinks-socket,sinks-file"
